# Everything a build should never carry, whichever of the three it is.
#
# `node_modules` first and by a distance: on this machine it is well over a
# gigabyte of symlinked pnpm store, and copying it into a context makes every
# build slow and every image wrong — the dependencies are installed from the
# lockfile inside the image instead.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv

.next
**/.next
**/staticfiles
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.turbo
**/.turbo

.git
.github

# Secrets, and the certificates mkcert issues. `.env.example` is committed and
# is the one that belongs in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
infra/coturn/certs

**/*.md
!README.md
